     "heading": "",
     "text": "Explainer · Compression How DEFLATE works The format inside gzip, zlib, PNG and ZIP is two simple ideas stacked on top of each other. First remove the repetition, then remove the skew. This page builds each one up, step by step, from a single 35-byte string. DEFLATE makes two separate savings. LZ77 replaces each repeat with a short (length, distance) pointer back to an earlier copy. Huffman coding then gives common symbols short bit patterns and rare ones long patterns. It matters because nearly everything uses it: gzip and zlib, PNG images, ZIP files, and Content-Encoding: gzip on the web. The common misconception is that the Huffman tree travels with the data. It doesn't. Only the code lengths are sent, and the codes are rebuilt from them by counting."
